WEBVTT

00:04.882 --> 00:07.578
- I'm gonna hate this movie.
- How can you be so sure?

00:08.685 --> 00:10.380
It's got subtitles.

00:10.554 --> 00:15.389
The only good subtitles are for Nazis,
Columbian drug lords and space aliens.

00:15.559 --> 00:17.390
Oh, and kung fu.

00:17.561 --> 00:19.961
&lt;i>Excuse me, but NPR called
Hiroshima, La Poubelle:&lt;/i>

00:20.130 --> 00:22.724
"An enchanting journey
of self-discovery."

00:22.900 --> 00:25.698
They're not gonna call it
"a two-hour French snoozefest...

00:25.869 --> 00:29.737
...for pompous douche buckets."
- You agreed if I paid for the tickets...

00:29.907 --> 00:31.534
...we could see what I wanna see.

00:32.042 --> 00:34.533
I didn't think
you could scrape together 18 bucks...

00:34.711 --> 00:36.440
...without stopping at a blood bank.

00:36.613 --> 00:39.411
It is a small price to pay
to get you out of the house.

00:39.583 --> 00:42.575
It's been three weeks since
you and Chelsea broke up. Move on.

00:42.753 --> 00:46.120
Says the guy who still carries around
a naked picture of his ex-wife.

00:46.290 --> 00:49.953
Hey, I bought those boobs, I have a right
to look at them once in a while.

00:53.463 --> 00:55.260
Damn. I don't believe it.

00:55.432 --> 00:56.956
- What?
- She's here.

00:57.134 --> 00:58.499
My ex-wife?

00:58.669 --> 01:01.069
No. It's Chelsea.

01:01.238 --> 01:02.569
She's with that Brad guy.

01:02.739 --> 01:05.139
So, what do we do? Do we say hello?

01:05.309 --> 01:07.641
No, we get the hell out of here.

01:07.811 --> 01:09.073
Charlie?

01:09.246 --> 01:12.010
Hey, look who's here.
Alan, Chelsea's here.

01:12.182 --> 01:13.911
Oh, hey, Chelsea.

01:14.084 --> 01:16.609
Hi, Alan. You guys remember Brad.

01:16.787 --> 01:18.914
- How's it going?
- Good, great.

01:19.089 --> 01:21.956
- Looking forward to the movie.
- I'm surprised to see you.

01:22.125 --> 01:24.150
This doesn't strike me
as your cup of tea.

01:24.328 --> 01:25.352
Are you kidding?

01:25.529 --> 01:28.760
NPR called it "an enchanting journey
of self-discovery."

01:28.932 --> 01:30.900
You know I live for that crap.

01:31.468 --> 01:34.699
Right.
Okay, well, it was good seeing you.

01:34.905 --> 01:36.600
You too.

01:39.109 --> 01:42.545
Wow, that was awkward.

01:43.347 --> 01:44.712
Tell me about it.

01:44.915 --> 01:46.177
Had to be tough for you.

01:46.350 --> 01:49.012
- Your ex-fiancée out with another guy.
- Uh-huh.

01:49.186 --> 01:51.677
- Good-looking guy.
- Yeah.

01:51.855 --> 01:54.050
You're here with your brother.

01:54.691 --> 01:57.626
- I know.
- That'll tighten the old sphincter.

01:59.429 --> 02:01.522
Oh, God.

02:01.698 --> 02:02.722
You still wanna go?

02:03.700 --> 02:05.998
No. No, I'm not gonna give her
the satisfaction.

02:06.169 --> 02:10.071
- I can suck it up for two hours.
- Three hours and 20 minutes.

02:10.574 --> 02:11.871
What?

02:12.042 --> 02:15.068
It covers four generations
of transsexual kabuki dancers.

02:18.949 --> 02:20.849
Let's go.

02:21.752 --> 02:25.813
All right. But I think you
should pay me back for the tickets.

02:26.023 --> 02:27.320
Well, not now.

02:28.725 --> 02:30.886
When it's convenient.

03:03.193 --> 03:05.661
I can't believe she's already dating.

03:05.829 --> 03:06.989
You're kidding, right?

03:07.164 --> 03:11.157
The day after she moved out, you ran off
to Vegas and married a stripper.

03:11.868 --> 03:14.234
- People grieve in different ways, Alan.
- Mm.

03:14.404 --> 03:17.862
Besides, the stripper was
already married, so no harm, no foul.

03:19.576 --> 03:21.134
Everybody's got somebody but me.

03:21.311 --> 03:23.211
Hello? I'm not with anyone either.

03:23.380 --> 03:27.009
Hello? You're a big loser
that says "Hello?"

03:31.788 --> 03:35.918
- I wonder if she's slept with him yet.
- Don't go there. Don't punish yourself.

03:36.093 --> 03:38.561
If she hasn't already,
I bet you she does tonight.

03:38.729 --> 03:40.492
Okay, punish yourself.

03:40.664 --> 03:43.531
What kind of man's gonna sit
through a gay French flick...

03:43.700 --> 03:46.863
...unless he figures he's got
a good shot of getting laid after?

03:47.037 --> 03:49.369
You didn't even give
that movie a chance.

03:50.040 --> 03:52.736
I bet you right now
he's driving her back to his place...

03:52.909 --> 03:55.503
...talking about the movie,
he'll make up some crap...

03:55.679 --> 03:57.078
...about how it made him cry.

03:57.247 --> 04:01.445
Then he'll ask her in for a cup of coffee,
which will turn into a glass of wine.

04:01.618 --> 04:04.109
One thing leads to another,
and before you know it...

04:04.321 --> 04:07.051
...he's got her in the bathtub
riding her like a Jet Ski.

04:09.359 --> 04:11.850
At least that's how I'd play it.

04:14.264 --> 04:16.061
- Come on.
- Where we going?

04:16.233 --> 04:18.565
Chelsea's. I gotta see
if she comes home tonight.

04:18.735 --> 04:20.259
Okay, why am I going?

04:20.437 --> 04:22.302
Hello? I'm hammered.

04:22.472 --> 04:25.908
How's it gonna look if I get a DUI
on the way to spy on my ex-girlfriend?

04:28.478 --> 04:32.039
He's very responsible
about drinking and stalking.

04:36.920 --> 04:39.388
How long are we gonna sit here?

04:39.589 --> 04:41.716
Till she comes home.

04:42.392 --> 04:44.383
What if she spends all night
with Brad?

04:44.895 --> 04:47.159
Well, then we'll be here all night.

04:47.731 --> 04:48.891
Hmm.

04:49.399 --> 04:50.957
No, no. No, don't:

04:51.134 --> 04:52.533
Hmm.

04:52.702 --> 04:55.000
Hey, I can "hmm" if I want to.

04:55.172 --> 04:57.265
- I'm tired.
- Then go to sleep.

04:57.440 --> 05:00.568
Without my melatonin and mouth guard?
I don't think so.

05:02.646 --> 05:05.308
Car. Car, car. Oh, it's them. It's them.

05:05.482 --> 05:07.973
- Get down. Get down.
- Okay. Okay. Quick, put this on.

05:08.151 --> 05:10.142
- What the hell is it?
- Mustache.

05:10.320 --> 05:14.086
- What are you doing with a mustache?
- Don't worry, it's fake.

05:14.491 --> 05:17.585
- That doesn't answer my question.
- Think you're the first guy...

05:17.761 --> 05:20.457
...who's checked up on a woman
who dumped you? Put it on.

05:20.630 --> 05:24.396
There is a whole side to you
I don't wanna know anything about.

05:25.502 --> 05:28.960
Hey, that's a good look for you.
It's kind of '70s porn star.

05:30.207 --> 05:31.299
I'm guessing.

05:34.144 --> 05:36.442
- Look at that thing he's driving.
- It's a Prius.

05:36.613 --> 05:40.709
Of course it's a Prius. "I'm saving the
planet, can I play with your boobies?"

05:40.917 --> 05:43.044
Hey. Hey, do not put down
the green lifestyle.

05:43.220 --> 05:46.053
I've worked hard to reduce
the size of my carbon footprint.

05:46.223 --> 05:49.920
You're a mooch and a miser,
don't try to make it sound hip.

05:50.961 --> 05:53.452
Wait, they're getting out of the car.

05:54.531 --> 05:58.831
Don't you just love how he dresses?
I mean, youthful, but not trying too hard.

05:59.002 --> 06:00.333
Unlike some people.

06:02.339 --> 06:04.000
Oh, great, they're kissing.

06:04.174 --> 06:06.938
Good thing he doesn't know
where her mouth has been.

06:10.814 --> 06:13.908
Wait a minute.
He's getting back in his car.

06:14.084 --> 06:15.574
And there he goes.

06:15.752 --> 06:20.018
Well, denied,
Mr. Greenpeace-Sissy-Pants.

06:20.390 --> 06:23.086
There. You feel better?
Can we please go home now?

06:23.260 --> 06:25.956
Just a minute.
I wanna make sure she gets inside okay.

06:26.363 --> 06:29.355
You know, there's a soft side to you
that I just applaud.

06:29.532 --> 06:33.832
You don't let it out very often, but when
you do, it just lights up the world.

06:35.472 --> 06:36.496
Wait a minute.

06:36.973 --> 06:39.942
Why is she getting in her car?
Where's she going at this hour?

06:40.110 --> 06:43.045
Maybe there's a third guy
and she's cheating on Brad.

06:43.213 --> 06:45.078
- What?
- Isn't that how you'd play it?

06:47.350 --> 06:49.215
Follow her.

06:51.888 --> 06:53.879
Catch up, catch up.
You're gonna lose her.

06:54.057 --> 06:57.254
Relax, this is not the first woman
I've surreptitiously followed...

06:57.427 --> 06:59.918
...while honoring the letter
of a restraining order.

07:01.998 --> 07:04.523
Oh, looks like she's heading
for Malibu.

07:04.701 --> 07:07.101
- Who does she know in Malibu?
- No idea.

07:08.939 --> 07:12.568
- What the hell is that?
- Oh, damn. I'm out of gas.

07:12.742 --> 07:14.801
- How could you be out of gas?
- I don't know.

07:15.011 --> 07:17.479
I just put $3 in the other day.

07:17.647 --> 07:19.046
Three dollars?

07:19.215 --> 07:22.241
Actually, 2.50. I bought a Milky Way.

07:22.419 --> 07:24.910
Oh, crap.

07:25.088 --> 07:27.750
All right, we'll just have to call AAA.

07:27.924 --> 07:29.289
Um...

07:29.759 --> 07:31.090
You don't have AAA?

07:31.261 --> 07:33.229
It costs like, $49 a year.

07:33.396 --> 07:35.421
Charlie, I gas up $3 at a time.

07:36.099 --> 07:37.828
Great. Just great.

07:38.034 --> 07:39.558
Do you have AAA?

07:39.736 --> 07:42.762
I have Mercedes Gold Platinum Valet
something or other.

07:42.939 --> 07:44.736
So? Won't they come help us?

07:45.408 --> 07:49.640
Let's see, will Mercedes come out
to put gas in an '89 Volvo?

07:49.813 --> 07:51.337
Let me call them to ask.

07:53.316 --> 07:55.784
You're actually waiting for me to call,
aren't you?

07:57.821 --> 07:59.584
No.

08:01.124 --> 08:03.285
Come on. We'll just have to hoof it.

08:03.460 --> 08:06.452
I'm supposed to leave my car
abandoned on the side of the road?

08:06.629 --> 08:08.290
What if somebody tries to steal it?

08:08.832 --> 08:12.666
Good thinking. Leave the keys,
gas money and a thank-you note.

08:13.870 --> 08:17.203
Spoken like someone with insurance.

08:21.911 --> 08:24.812
Ugh. My feet are killing me.

08:24.981 --> 08:28.314
Well, that's what you get for wearing
those expensive Italian loafers.

08:28.485 --> 08:31.977
- They're just not made for walking.
- You're right.

08:35.959 --> 08:38.018
- Hi, Charlie.
- Chels?

08:38.528 --> 08:41.326
Hey, Uncle Charlie,
you look like a '70s porn star.

08:44.367 --> 08:45.595
I'm guessing.

08:53.543 --> 08:54.908
What are you doing here?

08:55.078 --> 08:56.636
I needed to talk to you.

08:56.813 --> 08:58.804
Okay, what's up?

08:59.416 --> 09:00.747
Um...

09:01.184 --> 09:04.119
Oh, uh... Come on, Jake.
Let's give them some privacy.

09:04.287 --> 09:07.256
Why? Do you think
they're gonna do it on the couch?

09:11.761 --> 09:13.956
Okay, here it is.

09:16.466 --> 09:19.799
Seeing you tonight made me realize
how much I miss you.

09:20.070 --> 09:21.196
Really?

09:21.771 --> 09:22.795
Do you miss me?

09:22.972 --> 09:26.169
Oh, yeah.
He's been crying like a little girl.

09:26.342 --> 09:30.210
- Will you go away?
- What? I'm on your side.

09:31.948 --> 09:34.178
Well, I can see
nothing's changed around here.

09:34.350 --> 09:36.648
Well, just that you're gone.

09:36.820 --> 09:40.551
And yes, I do miss you
and I have been crying like a little girl.

09:40.723 --> 09:42.020
Good.

09:44.027 --> 09:45.824
So, what've you been up to?

09:47.197 --> 09:50.655
Not much. How do you like living
with your dad and his boyfriend?

09:51.234 --> 09:53.134
- It's a little weird.
- I can imagine.

09:53.303 --> 09:55.498
Two old Navy guys shacking up.

09:57.507 --> 09:58.735
The walls are pretty thin.

10:01.377 --> 10:04.835
Every night I'm hearing,
"Up periscope, down periscope.

10:07.317 --> 10:09.683
Launch the torpedo."

10:10.720 --> 10:13.382
Enough idle chitchat.
What's the deal with you and Brad?

10:13.556 --> 10:17.117
He's great, but it's just not the same.

10:18.027 --> 10:19.756
Have you two, uh?

10:20.363 --> 10:22.831
- No.
- Oh.

10:25.902 --> 10:28.234
Wipe that smile off your face.

10:28.404 --> 10:30.167
You wipe it off.

10:35.345 --> 10:37.336
You're gonna have to do
better than that.

10:44.020 --> 10:46.420
- One question.
- Yeah?

10:46.589 --> 10:48.056
What was with the mustache?

10:48.892 --> 10:52.589
When I'm out with Alan,
I don't like people to recognize me.

10:54.230 --> 10:57.097
Hey, they are doing it on the couch.

11:00.203 --> 11:02.637
So, what's the deal
with Uncle Charlie and Chelsea?

11:02.805 --> 11:05.797
Are they like back together
or was that just a booty call?

11:06.209 --> 11:10.669
- What do you know about booty calls?
- In theory, everything.

11:13.483 --> 11:15.314
Oh, crap.

11:15.485 --> 11:18.045
- What?
- Just a little disappointed.

11:18.221 --> 11:20.781
I saw Chelsea's car outside,
I didn't see yours.

11:24.394 --> 11:27.386
She spent the night.
We don't know if they're back together...

11:27.564 --> 11:29.794
...or if they're just scratching
the old itch.

11:29.966 --> 11:33.060
- What do you know about the "old itch"?
- It's intercourse, Dad.

11:33.236 --> 11:35.796
Why do we play these games?

11:38.641 --> 11:39.767
Good morning, all.

11:39.943 --> 11:41.740
Morning.

11:48.851 --> 11:51.342
- What?
- Come on, give.

11:51.521 --> 11:53.250
There's nothing to give.

11:53.423 --> 11:56.119
She came by,
said she misses me, spent the night.

11:56.292 --> 11:58.157
Yay.

11:59.495 --> 12:01.963
- So is she moving back in?
- Is the wedding back on?

12:02.131 --> 12:04.429
Or was it just
making the beast with two backs?

12:06.502 --> 12:08.629
What is wrong with you?

12:09.539 --> 12:11.530
I'm at an awkward age.

12:14.010 --> 12:15.477
- Morning, everyone.
- Morning.

12:15.645 --> 12:17.340
- Morning.
- Hey, you want coffee?

12:17.513 --> 12:19.344
I have to get home
and change for work.

12:19.515 --> 12:21.107
- Oh, okay.
- Can we talk?

12:21.284 --> 12:22.649
Sure.

12:23.286 --> 12:24.719
Oh, that's never good.

12:24.887 --> 12:27.947
- How do you know?
- That's what mom said to you.

12:30.159 --> 12:33.356
So I'm thinking you grab some things
from your dad's for tonight...

12:33.529 --> 12:35.724
...then we move your stuff back
this weekend.

12:35.898 --> 12:37.889
Charlie, I'm not coming back tonight.

12:38.067 --> 12:40.501
Well, why not?
Last night was good, right?

12:40.670 --> 12:43.798
It was great,
but it doesn't solve our problems.

12:44.173 --> 12:46.539
It sure solved mine.

12:47.577 --> 12:51.741
It's not that I don't love you, but I'm still
not sure that we have a future together.

12:51.914 --> 12:53.677
Chels, you're freaking me out here.

12:53.850 --> 12:56.512
- I've gotta go.
- No. Come on, wait.

12:56.686 --> 13:00.178
- Oh. I found your mustache.
- Where was it?

13:00.356 --> 13:02.881
Where do you think it was?
It was stuck to my ass.

13:14.737 --> 13:16.534
Hey.

13:16.706 --> 13:18.503
Hey.

13:19.676 --> 13:21.576
Feel like talking?

13:21.911 --> 13:25.074
- No, I do not.
- Understandable.

13:26.916 --> 13:31.319
You gotta admit, you're in a better place
now than you were this time last night.

13:32.255 --> 13:36.055
I mean, 24 hours ago, the woman you
love was out on a date with another man.

13:36.225 --> 13:40.753
But presto chango, she wound up
spending the night with you.

13:40.930 --> 13:45.367
Of course, come the morning, once again
she dropped you like a lead turd.

13:48.571 --> 13:49.595
Sorry.

13:50.773 --> 13:52.866
You didn't wanna talk.

13:57.714 --> 13:59.739
Me, I'm just the opposite.

14:00.249 --> 14:02.410
When I get my heart broken,
I have to talk.

14:02.585 --> 14:06.214
You cannot shut me up.
Yak, yak, yak, yak.

14:11.961 --> 14:13.485
Sorry.

14:18.668 --> 14:22.764
I've tried to be the strong silent type,
but, you know, it's just not who I am.

14:22.939 --> 14:25.635
I mean, not to mention
there's physical manifestations...

14:25.808 --> 14:30.245
...to bottling up your feelings.
I mean, constipation, migraines.

14:30.413 --> 14:34.179
Or it goes the other way, gas, diarrhea.

14:35.017 --> 14:36.746
You just cannot predict it.

14:36.919 --> 14:39.285
It's kind of an emotional crapshoot.

14:45.428 --> 14:47.191
Crapshoot.

14:47.997 --> 14:50.465
That just came to me.
Right off the top of my head.

14:52.468 --> 14:53.696
Got it.

14:58.007 --> 14:59.770
But you are lucky.

15:00.543 --> 15:02.807
You've got your music
to express your feelings.

15:02.979 --> 15:06.415
I mean, you could play the blues,
for instance.

15:07.950 --> 15:10.544
&lt;i>Bum, buh, duh, duh&lt;/i>

15:10.720 --> 15:12.347
&lt;i>My baby done left me&lt;/i>

15:14.690 --> 15:16.681
&lt;i>Bum, buh, duh, duh&lt;/i>

15:16.859 --> 15:18.622
&lt;i>She ain't coming back&lt;/i>

15:23.533 --> 15:25.831
&lt;i>Bum, buh, duh, duh&lt;/i>

15:26.335 --> 15:27.359
What's going on?

15:27.804 --> 15:29.431
&lt;i>I'm smothering your daddy&lt;/i>

15:29.605 --> 15:31.869
&lt;i>Bum, buh, duh, duh&lt;/i>

15:43.519 --> 15:47.182
I'm just saying it seems like every time
it's my turn to pick up the crap...

15:47.356 --> 15:48.823
...he's got the runs.

15:48.991 --> 15:51.186
So stop feeding him chili.

15:52.595 --> 15:54.153
- Oh, hey, Charlie.
- Hey, Charlie.

15:54.330 --> 15:55.490
Hey, Tom. Ed.

15:55.665 --> 15:56.825
You looking for Chelsea?

15:56.999 --> 16:00.196
No, he came to see
two old queens walking a dog.

16:00.369 --> 16:03.395
Who you calling a queen, Elizabeth?

16:03.573 --> 16:06.872
She's not here, Charlie.
- She went to dinner with that Brad guy.

16:07.043 --> 16:08.067
Oh.

16:08.277 --> 16:11.371
- Wanna come in? Have a beer?
- No, I don't wanna bother you guys.

16:11.547 --> 16:13.208
Don't be silly, come on.

16:13.382 --> 16:15.373
Okay. Thanks.

16:16.285 --> 16:20.346
- You had to tell him she's with Brad?
- What, I'm supposed to lie?

16:20.523 --> 16:24.050
No, but you can dummy up.
I mean, look at the poor bastard.

16:26.762 --> 16:29.424
Yeah. Jeez, I'm sorry.
I wasn't thinking.

16:29.599 --> 16:32.534
"I wasn't thinking."
That should be your middle name.

16:33.002 --> 16:36.870
Don't be getting in my face
when I'm holding a bag of poop.

16:39.809 --> 16:43.643
- I'll grab some brews.
- Chelsea told me about last night.

16:43.813 --> 16:46.748
I don't understand it, Tom.
I thought we were back together.

16:46.916 --> 16:49.544
Yeah, well,
you can't make sense out of a woman.

16:49.719 --> 16:52.210
They're like beautiful puzzles
with missing pieces...

16:52.388 --> 16:54.379
...or a great book with no ending.

16:54.557 --> 16:58.323
Or like my old man used to say,
"They're all frigging nuts."

17:00.396 --> 17:03.797
I don't know what to do. Should I
leave her alone? Should I pursue her?

17:03.966 --> 17:09.427
If I might chime in, I would say
that stopping by unannounced...

17:09.605 --> 17:14.440
...with some liquor-store flowers
sends up a rather desperate flare.

17:14.844 --> 17:16.311
I know. I know.

17:16.479 --> 17:20.142
I just couldn't sit home and do nothing.
I keep turning it over in my mind.

17:20.316 --> 17:23.080
What did I do wrong?
What could I have done differently?

17:23.252 --> 17:27.018
Man, how many times did I ask myself
that question when I was married?

17:27.189 --> 17:28.315
Me too.

17:28.491 --> 17:32.587
What do we got between the two of us?
Something like 80 years of marriage?

17:32.762 --> 17:37.324
Let's see, I was with Beth for 38
and you were with Martha for 40, 41...

17:37.500 --> 17:40.367
I didn't need you
to actually do the math.

17:40.570 --> 17:43.038
Don't bark at me.
I'll beat the snot out of you.

17:43.205 --> 17:45.503
Bring it on, mister.

17:47.176 --> 17:48.336
Maybe I should go.

17:48.511 --> 17:50.479
No, no, no. Sit down, finish your beer.

17:50.646 --> 17:53.843
- We're just sparring.
- I love this broken-down son of a bitch.

17:54.016 --> 17:57.452
Oh, for God's sake,
don't gay it up in front of company.

17:57.954 --> 17:59.649
Now, you listen to me, young man.

17:59.822 --> 18:03.451
In the final analysis, it doesn't matter
what you did or didn't do.

18:03.626 --> 18:04.820
You want Chelsea back?

18:04.994 --> 18:07.861
You've gotta make her miss you
like she did last night.

18:08.030 --> 18:11.193
She's not gonna miss you
if you're squatting in her living room...

18:11.367 --> 18:13.028
...with those sad-ass petunias.

18:13.669 --> 18:16.399
So what? I'm supposed to just
go about my business...

18:16.606 --> 18:19.074
...hoping one day she shows up
and says "I'm back"?

18:19.241 --> 18:21.209
Or you can do like me and Ed did.

18:21.377 --> 18:23.709
Change teams.

18:25.047 --> 18:27.311
A lot easier living with a man
than a woman.

18:27.984 --> 18:31.147
Tom and I watch the same TV shows,
we like the same food.

18:31.320 --> 18:33.311
You don't have to leave the room
to fart.

18:33.489 --> 18:37.186
You don't have to,
but it sure would be a nice idea.

18:39.629 --> 18:44.066
Okay, well, thanks, fellas.
This was real helpful.

18:44.567 --> 18:47.365
- We're always here for you, Charlie.
- Thank you.

18:47.536 --> 18:50.334
- Don't tell Chelsea I stopped by.
- I wouldn't dream of it.

18:50.506 --> 18:52.940
Remember what we told you.
Lay low for a while.

18:53.142 --> 18:56.134
- Run silent, run deep.
- There you go.

19:00.683 --> 19:02.207
Well, what do you think?

19:02.385 --> 19:05.877
Watch SportsCenter
and then fool around a little?

19:06.455 --> 19:10.084
You need to take a Viagra?

19:10.693 --> 19:12.126
You're my Viagra, baby.

19:12.294 --> 19:14.728
Aww. That's so sweet.

19:14.897 --> 19:16.762
Just for that, you can hold the remote.

19:28.210 --> 19:29.268
Hey.

19:29.445 --> 19:32.676
Sorry, I didn't mean to disturb you.
Just grabbing a water.

19:32.848 --> 19:35.442
No, no, no. It's fine. Come on, join me.

19:40.923 --> 19:41.947
Really?

19:42.124 --> 19:44.115
Yeah. Sit down.

19:45.728 --> 19:47.662
Okay.

19:51.967 --> 19:57.132
Listen, I wanna apologize for,
you know...

19:57.306 --> 19:59.638
Trying to kill me with a pillow?

20:00.710 --> 20:03.679
It was horseplay,
don't make a big thing about it.

20:03.846 --> 20:07.680
What I'm saying is that
I know you were trying to cheer me up...

20:07.850 --> 20:09.010
...and I appreciate it.

20:10.453 --> 20:11.750
Thank you.

20:12.655 --> 20:17.251
I realize that I give you a hard time
about living here...

20:17.460 --> 20:23.228
...but frankly, it's probably a good thing
for me to have you around.

20:25.234 --> 20:30.536
Wow. Charlie, that means so much
to hear you say that.

20:31.774 --> 20:33.469
Well...

20:35.111 --> 20:38.080
I do... I do love you, buddy.

20:40.683 --> 20:42.981
And I love you too.

20:45.054 --> 20:46.351
I know, I know.

20:46.522 --> 20:49.491
I don't want this moment to ever end.

20:52.194 --> 20:53.218
Okay.

20:53.395 --> 20:55.863
I mean it. I am not letting go.

20:56.499 --> 20:59.900
Well, you're gonna have to
because it's starting to get a little weird.

21:00.069 --> 21:03.095
We don't need women,
we've got each other.

21:03.939 --> 21:07.136
All right, you brought this on yourself.

21:08.611 --> 21:13.048
Don't worry,
I'll wait for you on the other side.
